{"kind":"assert","text":"Ruling on 361bb699: accept the split for head G item 1. Typed\nauthoring sources stay offline, and the runtime reads generated\ndata.\n\n1. The authoritative source of the Grow Room, the Grow Site, base\n   Change and Issue is typed authoring code that uses the define\n   package: `authoring/{forms,room,site}` for Grow and\n   `authoring/{shared,change,issue}` for the lanes.\n2. No runtime path imports the define package or an authoring\n   module by value. That covers simulator-host, demo-definitions,\n   the Card and dap-lanes. A type-only import is allowed.\n3. The existing offline pin scripts compile the authoring sources\n   and write the generated data. The normal check writes nothing.\n   It compares the rendered data and the pins that F migrated,\n   byte for byte.\n4. The hand-rolled construction goes: the Grow component builders\n   and the lanes' shared construction. Projections, types and the\n   historical descendants stay. The define fixtures become\n   re-exports, so one authored model remains for each definition.\n5. The lane producer generates each parent before it imports a\n   descendant, as you say.\n\nOne amendment: keep one generated artifact for each definition.\nThe lanes already hold `definitions/*.json`. Where a runtime export\ncan read that JSON and take its type from the authoring module by\na type-only import, do that, and add no generated TypeScript beside\nit. Use generated literal TypeScript only where a consumer needs\nliteral types that the type-only import cannot give, or where its\nbuild cannot import JSON. Say in the note which form each\ndefinition uses and why. Do not ask again for that choice.\n\nHead G changes no pin and adds no runtime dependency. The whole\n`scripts/active-source.test.mjs` owner is in the focused run, as\nfor every head.","body":{"to":"feb90d36627c7f4466ef9473c4fa0bbaf91699d16b93d832a37629988dfba6de"}}